# An .npmignore (NOT a `files` allowlist) is REQUIRED here: with a `files` field
# npm STOPS honoring .npmignore and would re-ship the vitest suites (the exact
# trap the CLI publish-readiness guard documents; web uses this same pattern).
# Relying on .npmignore alone keeps tests out of the tarball while still
# shipping the TS source that press-web imports at runtime and press-cms bundles.
node_modules/
vitest.config.ts
**/*.test.ts
